# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings, even when checked out on Windows.
#
# A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist. Inside a Linux container that surfaces as
# the deeply unhelpful:
#
#   exec /kong-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# ...for a file that is plainly there. This broke the Kong gateway on a
# Windows dev machine and would have broken any deployment building from a
# Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else executed by a Linux container.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint* text eol=lf
